Feature: Full Video Processing Pipeline
  As a BIT Platform Operator
  I want a complete end-to-end video processing pipeline
  So that video content can be split, surfaces detected, brand-safety checked, assets associated, scenes approved, rendered, stitched into a final continuous video, invoiced, and downloaded.

  Scenario: Scene Cut Detection and Video Splitting
    Given a raw broadcast video content item in Staging state
    When the detection pipeline is executed
    Then the video is split into discrete SceneItems with valid start frame, end frame, duration, and keyframe thumbnail.

  Scenario: AI Engine Selection and Brand Safety Exclusions
    Given detected candidate surfaces in a scene
    When brand-safety check is evaluated against permanent exclusion policies
    Then surfaces with faces, emergency vehicles, or competitor brands are tagged as Excluded with an ExclusionReason
    And candidate surfaces are marked as Unchecked.

  Scenario: Asset Association and Approval Gate
    Given an Unchecked candidate surface
    When an operator approves the ad placement and associates a campaign creative asset
    Then the surface status changes to Approved
    And an ApprovalItem audit record is recorded
    And unapproved surfaces block render dispatch.

  Scenario: Video Rendering, Scene Rejoining, and Download
    Given an approved surface with an associated creative asset
    When a render job is dispatched
    Then individual scene frames are composited via homography transformation
    And all scenes are stitched together via FFmpeg concat filter into a single full-length video file
    And the final continuous video file can be downloaded via the download endpoint.

  Scenario: Campaign Invoice Calculation
    Given an active campaign with approved placements and render jobs
    When the campaign invoice summary is requested
    Then an invoice is calculated based on placement exposure duration, surface viability scores, and render processing fees.
